WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Set one ISSM solver limit, review it, then launch explicitly.
Why: Use the reviewed BYO workflow for one native ISSM solver change.
Look for: Example: canonical SquareIceShelf; stressbalance iteration cap 120.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Describe the change: Set stressbalance max iterations to 120.
Why: A narrow request makes the proposed change easy to verify.
Look for: Keep the model, example and Cloud execution mode.

3
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Choose Create plan. Read the proposed value of 120.
Why: A plan proposes a change; it does not start the solver.
Look for: Expected: one change; no override → 120.

4
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Apply the reviewed 120 limit to the launch form.
Why: Apply only after confirming 120 and the retained experiment.
Look for: Expected: Configuration updated · 1 setting changed.

5
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Choose Review in Advanced to inspect the native controls.
Why: The native form is where you review execution controls.
Look for: Continue to the normal launch form.

6
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:07.000
Confirm ISSM → SquareIceShelf.
Why: The change should not select a different scientific example.
Look for: The canonical example is retained.

7
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Confirm Action Run and target runme.m.
Why: runme.m retains the canonical scientific entrypoint.
Look for: The native canonical entrypoint is retained.

8
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Read the native review: ISSM · SquareIceShelf.
Why: Review before submitting so the new run uses the intended example.
Look for: Check the reviewed model and example before submission.

9
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Scroll to Infrastructure. Check that every row is Ready.
Why: Storage, image, license and compute must be ready before submission.
Look for: Account, storage, image and compute must be ready.

10
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:49.000
Choose Launch cloud run only after the final review.
Why: This explicit action starts the native cloud execution.
Look for: This explicit action submits the native job.

11
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Wait for the new SquareIceShelf run to submit.
Why: Follow the new run before inspecting its outputs.
Look for: The current run changes from staging to submitting.

12
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:09.000
Open Results. Choose StressbalanceSolution and Vel.
Why: The selected field must belong to the completed run.
Look for: The completed native result contains 91 nodal velocity values.

13
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Choose Render.
Why: Render updates the displayed field; it does not rerun the solver.
Look for: Expected: native velocity field, 0–9034.39 m/year.

14
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:36.000
Choose Download results. Wait for the new archive link.
Why: Package the mesh, fields, figure and runtime provenance together.
Look for: A fresh results_bundle link appears for this run.

15
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:49.000
Choose the fresh results_bundle link to save it.
Why: The fresh link saves the archive prepared for this run.
Look for: Keep the native outputs and runtime provenance together.

16
00:02:49.000 --> 00:03:01.000
Inspect the saved native velocity figure.
Why: The colorbar and solver record explain the result in physical units.
Look for: ISSM converged in 23 iterations, below both caps of 100 and 120.

17
00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:14.000
Compare the retained mesh and fields with the Basic result.
Why: Convergence below both caps explains this unchanged recorded result.
Look for: For this changed-cap case, every compared numeric value was exactly equal.
